In classic World of Warcraft, most warlocks are seen with Voidwalkers because the Succubus's **Seduction** ability is a charm effect that breaks on any damage taken. This makes it unreliable in chaotic group combat or while questing, where accidental damage from AoE or other players frequently breaks the charm. Voidwalkers, by contrast, provide consistent tanking and threat generation without this fragility.

The hint refers to the fact that Seduction is often perceived as a powerful crowd-control tool, but its fragility makes it less practical for general leveling and questing compared to the Voidwalker's durability. [end of text]


